TinyGL for the S31 libGL
========================

Origin
------
Vendored from erysdren TinyGL (https://github.com/erysdren/TinyGL), commit
7f229c8 ("ui: blit to texture for sdl2/sdl3"), MIT (COPYING, also LICENSE).
It is Fabrice Bellard's TinyGL 0.4.1 plus erysdren's arrays/ortho/offscreen
work. The source layout is kept (include/, source/, examples/) so a diff
against the upstream checkout reads directly:

    git clone https://github.com/erysdren/TinyGL && git -C TinyGL checkout 7f229c8
    diff -ru TinyGL/source gl/tinygl/source

Not vendored: archive/ (the 0.4 / 0.4.1 tarballs) and .github/.
Not built: source/glu.c (plan 2.3: GLU is Mesa's libGLU, unmodified) and
source/ostinygl.c (replaced by source/s31_ctx.c).

This directory is the rasteriser core only. The public, Khronos-ABI GL
entry points are gl/api/; GLX is gl/glx/; the build is gl/build.sh (RV32)
and gl/host-build.sh (host rig).

How the two headers coexist
---------------------------
TinyGL compiles against its own include/GL/gl.h; gl/api compiles against
the standard headers in gl/include/GL (libglvnd/Mesa, MIT). They meet only
through source/tgl_bridge.h, which uses plain C types and is included by
zgl.h too, so every bridge declaration is checked against TinyGL's
definition by the compiler.

- Every TinyGL entry point is renamed tgl_<name> (include/GL/tgl_rename.h,
  included first by gl.h) and TinyGL is built -fvisibility=hidden, so the
  ABI layer is the only exporter of GL names.
- Enum VALUES are shared: gl/api/enumcmp.py checks every GL_* in TinyGL's
  gl.h against the Khronos headers and fails the build on a mismatch. Two
  were wrong upstream and are fixed here: GL_POLYGON_OFFSET_FACTOR (0x3038,
  Khronos 0x8038) and GL_ALL_ATTRIB_BITS (0x000fffff, Khronos 0xffffffff).
  Names TinyGL lacked were added with their Khronos values ("s31 additions"
  at the end of the enum).
- glFrustum, glOrtho and glClearDepth take float internally (double is a
  libgcc call on this F-without-D hart); the ABI layer converts with
  s31_float.h's s31_d2f, bit-exact with (float)d (gl/tests/d2f_test.c).

Changes (every changed site is marked "s31")
--------------------------------------------
Robustness - TinyGL exit(1)ed or asserted on ordinary stock-app input:
- error.c: gl_fatal_error no longer exits; prints once per message. Every
  caller returns safely and records the GL error the spec gives.
- a real GL error flag (GLContext.error; first error sticks until
  glGetError); asserts replaced by GL_INVALID_ENUM / _VALUE / _OPERATION,
  GL_STACK_OVERFLOW / _UNDERFLOW (matrix and name stacks: the asserts had
  been the only bounds checks), GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY.
- list.c: list names are bounds-checked (the table was indexed with any
  value), glGenLists starts at 1, undefined lists are ignored (GL) instead
  of exiting, nesting is capped at 64, glNewList/glEndList misuse errors.
- texture.c: see "Textures" below; glGenTextures reserves its names (two
  calls returned the same name); a texture with no image draws untextured
  (clip.c read a NULL pixmap).
- vertex.c: glBegin(bad mode), nested glBegin, glEnd without glBegin, and a
  failed vertex-array growth no longer abort.
- api.c: colours are clamped to [0,1] before the integer flat colour is
  made (out-of-range colours wrapped); lights, materials and light models
  read only as many floats as the pname has.

Buffers and contexts (s31_ctx.c, see gl/api/s31gl.h for the contract):
- Rendering goes straight into the caller's RGB565 buffer of any pitch
  (ZBuffer.linesize = pitch); no ZB_copyFrameBuffer. zline.h stepped rows
  by xsize pixels instead of linesize bytes - wrong for any pitched buffer,
  it wrote outside it - and is fixed.
- The depth buffer is allocated at the first clear/draw, not at bind.
- The GLX frame hook runs once per frame before the first access
  (gl_prepare in zgl.h; one load and branch per glBegin/glClear).
- Several contexts, with glXCreateContext list/texture sharing (refcounted
  GLSharedState); with nothing current, GL calls go to a buffer-less
  context and are dropped. endSharedState/glClose free every list, texture
  chain and specular table (TinyGL leaked all but the first of each).
- misc.c/vertex.c, the viewport guard: GL's viewport is bottom-up and may
  be larger than, or lie outside, the window. TinyGL measured from the top
  and relied on resizing its own buffer to the viewport. gl_eval_viewport
  now intersects the viewport with the buffer and, when it is not wholly
  inside, folds a clip-space scale/offset into the projection so the
  ordinary clipper cuts primitives to the visible part - exact screen
  positions, nothing written outside, zero per-pixel cost.
  gl/tests/core_test.c fuzzes it (20000 random viewports and primitives
  with canaries round the buffer).
- memset_16 aligns before word stores (odd-width rows start 2 bytes off);
  a contiguous colour buffer is cleared in one pass.

State (s31_state.c, get.c): every GL 1.3 fixed-function value is recorded
for glGet* / glIsEnabled, validated, and list-compilable (one new opcode,
OP_State). What the rasteriser HONOURS today (plan F3-F6, 2026-09-26):

  honoured      depth test with all 8 functions and glDepthMask on every
                primitive; glDepthRange; glClearDepth (clear.c: stored as
                (1 - d) * 0xffff since Z grows towards the viewer); blending
                (every GL 1.3 factor; destination alpha is 1, there is no
                alpha plane); glAlphaFunc (all 8); glColorMask (drawing and
                glClear); fog LINEAR/EXP/EXP2; glScissor (drawing and
                glClear); glPolygonOffset (GL_FILL); glLineWidth and
                glPointSize (nearest integer when aliased, exact when
                smooth); the texture
                environments REPLACE, MODULATE (the default), DECAL, BLEND
                (with GL_TEXTURE_ENV_COLOR) and ADD for every base format;
                GL_CLAMP / GL_CLAMP_TO_EDGE / GL_REPEAT; GL_SEPARATE_SPECULAR_
                COLOR; GL_RESCALE_NORMAL; texture completeness (an
                incomplete texture is off, as GL 3.8.10 says); the stencil
                test, ops and clears with an 8-bit stencil buffer, and none
                of it without one (phase 4 F8, below); glBlendEquation(
                Separate) and glBlendFuncSeparate (phase 4 BLEND-EQ);
                GL_LINE_SMOOTH and GL_POINT_SMOOTH (phase 4 SMOOTH);
                glHint; GL_DITHER/GL_MULTISAMPLE (no effect by definition);
                GL_LIGHT_MODEL_TWO_SIDE (the back material and -n on
                back-facing polygons, light.c / clip.c; it was |n.l| on the
                front material); glPushAttrib(GL_TEXTURE_BIT) with the bound
                objects' filters, wraps, border colour and priority.
  approximated  (prints "libGL: approximated ..." once; tools/glref does not
                count it as a gap) since phase 4, only details of the
                texture filters (see "Phase 4" below): one mipmap level
                (lambda) per triangle, NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR as nearest in
                the nearer level, GL_CLAMP under a linear filter as
                CLAMP_TO_EDGE.
                Not printed: the texture q (glTexCoord4, texgen Q) divides
                s and t per vertex - exact when q is the same at every
                vertex of a primitive; where it varies (projective
                texturing) s/q, t/q are interpolated with 1/w's perspective,
                not q/w's. Fragment alpha is 8 bits, so the alpha test
                compares a/255 with the reference exactly (texels are
                exact) but cannot tell a vertex alpha of 0.5 from 128/255
                (raster_sel.c). Fog is per vertex (EXP/EXP2 differ from
                Mesa's per-fragment fog on large polygons); Gouraud colour
                is linear in screen space except where that is visibly
                wrong (phase 4 F-PERSP, below).
                Plan F7 (2026-09-26, see "Pixel paths" below): the raster
                position, glBitmap, glDrawPixels, glReadPixels,
                glCopyPixels, glCopyTexImage/SubImage 1D/2D, glPixelZoom,
                glPixelTransfer scale/bias, texgen S/T/R (OBJECT_LINEAR,
                EYE_LINEAR, SPHERE_MAP), six user clip planes, polygon and
                line stipple, 1D textures, glGetTexImage.
  recorded only (prints "libGL: unimplemented ..." once when used):
                logic op, smooth polygons (drawn aliased),
                GL_DOT3_RGB/RGBA (GL_INVALID_ENUM, not advertised: the
                combiner is ARB_texture_env_combine's, not GL 1.3's
                texture_env_dot3), 3D/cube textures, texture
                borders (dropped), GL_NORMAL_MAP / GL_REFLECTION_MAP
                texgen (cube maps), GL_MAP_COLOR (pixel maps; glPixelMap
                is a stub), glDrawPixels(GL_COLOR_INDEX), the evaluators
                (glMap*, glEvalMesh*: GLU's NURBS draws through them) and
                feedback. These are the plan's F8.

Rasteriser paths (raster.c, raster_sel.c, zpipe.h/zpipe.c,
ztriangle_gen.c). gl_update_raster runs at glBegin when any state that
matters changed (c->raster_dirty) and picks, once per batch, never per
pixel:
- tier 1: TinyGL's own fused fillers (ztriangle.c), their per-pixel loops
  unchanged,
  for untextured flat/smooth triangles and textures whose environment is
  the texel (REPLACE/DECAL of an opaque texture, MODULATE by a white vertex
  colour - checked per triangle), REPEAT wrap, depth LEQUAL (TinyGL's >=,
  with or without the write), strict LESS (ztriangle_lt.c) or off, and no
  blending, alpha test, fog or colour mask. A frame that uses no new
  feature runs only this; gl/bench/BASELINE.md has the proof.
- the general path: a fixed list of stage functions chosen for the state
  (depth test -> colour -> texel index -> texenv -> colour sum -> fog ->
  alpha test -> depth write -> blend/mask/store), each a straight loop over
  a 32-pixel chunk. A disabled feature has no stage. Every attribute is a
  plane equation; textures and fog are divided by w (perspective-correct).
  Lines and points take it too when textured, wide, depth-masked or with
  any fragment feature; line pixels are gathered into spans (raster.c
  gl_general_line: ~125 instructions a blended pixel, was ~310).
ONE scan conversion for both (ztri.h; review P1/G1, 2026-09-26). GL 1.3
Appendix A rule 2: changing blend, alpha test, depth function or mask must
not change the fragments a primitive generates or their depth - and those
are the state changes that move a triangle between the paths. Both
therefore take coverage and depth from ztri_setup: GL window coordinates
(zp.fx/fy, not TinyGL's snapped x/y), pixel centres, the top-left rule (a
mesh covers each pixel once; TinyGL's inclusive spans drew shared edges
twice, which blending shows), 16.16 edges stepped from each edge's own
first row (so triangles sharing an edge agree to the bit), and one integer
depth plane per triangle, z = zc + dzdx x + dzdy y. The float code feeding
those integers uses explicit fmaf, so -ffp-contract cannot make two inlined
copies differ. Multipass (an opaque pass on tier 1, then GL_EQUAL or
LEQUAL blended on the general path: TyrQuake's lightmaps) lands on the
same pixels, and meshes that mix paths per triangle have no cracks:
gl/tests/raster_gate.c checks both, and the texel phase below.
Textures on both paths sample the texel under the pixel centre (GL
nearest): TinyGL's [0,1] "texture squeeze", which hid the missing centre
offset, is gone (review G2: a 1:1 RGB texture sampled the neighbouring row
over half the image), and a triangle with a negative REPEAT coordinate is
moved by whole periods so the int conversion floors. q = 1/w is computed
once per vertex (review P2; the per-triangle copies and divides are gone).
Lines and size-1 points use the pixel holding the vertex's GL window
position (TinyGL's (w - 1/2)/2 mapping was up to 1.25 px from it, beyond
what polygon offset covers for lines drawn over an offset fill). Facing
and polygon offset read the float position too: the snapped one called
sub-pixel triangles degenerate and dropped them, a crack now that
neighbours no longer overlap.
Measured on the host rig against Mesa: gl/tests/glx_raster.c (6 pages of
feature cells, gl/tests/run-raster.sh), ASan/UBSan clean
(gl/tests/run-san.sh).

Textures (texture.c, s31_pixels.c), plan F3: every texture is stored at
its own power-of-two size up to GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE 256 - RGB565, plus an
A8 plane only when the format has alpha (ALPHA, LUMINANCE_ALPHA,
INTENSITY, RGBA and 2/4; gl/bench/texfmt.c measured it against ARGB4444).
Non-power-of-two or larger than 256 is GL_INVALID_VALUE, as GL 1.1 says,
with one "libGL:" line; the proxy answers what a real upload would accept
(GLU's gluBuild2DMipmaps depends on it). glTexImage2D and glTexSubImage2D
accept every GL 1.3 format/type in s31_pixels.c and honour every
GL_UNPACK_* parameter; inside glNewList the pixels are unpacked at compile
time and the list owns the copy. Levels > 0 are validated and recorded
(completeness, glGetTexLevelParameter) and, since phase 4, stored and
filtered (below). The fixed-point s/t layout keeps GL_REPEAT to masks, the
same three operations per pixel as TinyGL's 256x256 constants (zbuffer.h);
|texcoord| up to 512 repeats is exact. Level L is at most 256 >> L, for
proxies and real uploads (review G3: GLU's closestFit probes level 1, and a
level-blind proxy made gluBuild2DMipmaps of a 384 or 512 image return
success with no texture); a proxy remembers its level and border. The
common uploads (UNSIGNED_BYTE RGB, RGBA, LUMINANCE, no pixel transfer) are
converted straight from the client's bytes, one loop per stored class
(review P7: 12-17 instructions a texel, were 25-31). A texture object is
152 bytes on RV32 (was 288): one stored image, not MAX_TEXTURE_LEVELS,
and a pointer to the levels > 0 (phase 4).

Pixel paths (plan F7: s31_draw.c, s31_pixels.c, s31_rpos.c, s31_xform.c;
gl/api/gl_pixels.c):
- glRasterPos* goes through the modelview and projection with GL's own
  viewport transform (the full viewport, window y up); a position outside
  the view volume or a user clip plane is invalid, and invalid positions
  drop glBitmap (no move either) and glDrawPixels / glCopyPixels. The
  raster colour is the lit colour when lighting is on (the secondary colour
  folded in: there is no colour sum on the pixel paths), texcoords take
  texgen and the texture matrix, GL_CURRENT_RASTER_DISTANCE is the eye
  distance. glWindowPos* (GL 1.4, ARB and MESA names, MESA's 4-component
  ones) set it directly. All are compiled into display lists; glBitmap and
  glDrawPixels unpack their data at compile time and the list owns the copy.
- Fragments of glBitmap / glDrawPixels / glCopyPixels take the raster
  depth, the raster texcoords' texel and |z_e| fog, and pass the same
  per-fragment stages as primitives (zpipe.c: depth, texenv, fog, alpha,
  blend, colour mask; not the polygon stipple). The stage list is derived
  from the general path's and cached per context (c->pixpipe, keyed by
  pipe_serial). With no fragment operation enabled - bitmap text, 2D
  overlays - pixels are stored directly. Pixel rectangles clip to the
  buffer and the scissor box, never to the viewport.
- glBitmap: every GL_UNPACK_* parameter for GL_BITMAP (LSB_FIRST,
  SKIP_PIXELS in bits, ROW_LENGTH, ALIGNMENT); placed at floor(raster -
  origin + 1e-4), as Mesa does; a row is read 32 pixels at a time and its
  runs found with ctz. gl/bench/pix.sh: 8x13 glyphs cost ~2.3 k
  instructions each with nothing enabled, ~6.6 k blended.
- glDrawPixels: every format/type s31_pixels.c unpacks, GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT
  (depth fragments with the raster colour), glPixelZoom by GL's pixel-
  square rule (any factor, negative flips). GL_STENCIL_INDEX is
  GL_INVALID_OPERATION (no stencil buffer).
- glReadPixels: from the one colour buffer (the back buffer the next swap
  presents; GL_READ_BUFFER is recorded, not honoured), RGB565 expanded
  with rounding (v * 255 / 31); every GL_PACK_* parameter, the GL 1.3
  formats (LUMINANCE = R + G + B, clamped), types including the packed
  ones and FLOAT, GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT; only the part inside the buffer is
  written. Not compiled into lists (GL 5.4).
- glPixelTransfer scale and bias apply on every path: glDrawPixels,
  glTexImage/SubImage (teapot), glReadPixels, glCopyPixels, glCopyTexImage.
- glCopyTexImage2D/1D and glCopyTexSubImage2D/1D read the colour buffer
  when they execute (compiled into lists as commands).
- Texgen (s31_xform.c): per vertex only when enabled - it rides on the
  apply_texture_matrix test glopVertex already made; sphere map uses the
  eye normal (normalised under GL_NORMALIZE) and the unit eye position.
- User clip planes: stored in eye coordinates (glGetClipPlane), tested in
  clip space (plane times the inverse of the projection in use, so clipper-
  made vertices need nothing extra); clip-code bits 6..11 in clip.c for
  triangles, lines and points. The per-vertex test is behind the vtx_extra
  test that replaced raster_fog: nothing added to a frame without them.
- Polygon stipple: a stage of the general path (zpipe.c), polygons only,
  the depth write moved after it; the pattern unpacked per GL_UNPACK_*.
  Line stipple: the general line path; the counter restarts per GL_LINES
  segment and at a strip's first segment, runs on along a strip, and is
  counted from the first vertex. Both force the general path only while
  enabled.
- 1D textures (texture.c): their own binding and default object; stored
  as W x 1 and drawn by the same paths (GL_TEXTURE_2D wins when both are
  enabled). glGetTexImage reads levels > 0 as what is drawn (level 0
  sampled at the level's size).
- Known differences from Mesa llvmpipe, by design: Mesa draws neither fog
  on glBitmap nor on glDrawPixels (its bitmap quad carries fog coordinate
  0); GL 3.10 says the fragments are fogged, as here. Mesa's bitmap cache
  draws a cached glBitmap with state changed after the call (gl/tests/
  glx_pixels.c flushes around state changes so its reference is GL's).
  Lines keep TinyGL's inclusive last pixel (GL's diamond rule drops it).
Tests: gl/tests/glx_pixels.c (4 pages) and gl/tests/glu_check.c (the real
Mesa GLU: Debian's libglu1-mesa, statically, and the board's GLU 9.0.3)
against Mesa by gl/tests/run-pixels.sh; gl/tests/core_test.c test_f7.

Vertex arrays (arrays.c, rewritten): byte strides (0 = packed), every GL
1.1 type (colour as UNSIGNED_BYTE, GL_DOUBLE via s31_d2f), the edge-flag
array; client state executes at once and is never compiled; glDrawArrays /
glDrawElements / glArrayElement inside glNewList compile the vertices, not
the pointers. Fixed: the normal array wrote Z twice; an array colour left
the flat-shading integer colour as stack garbage.

Also fixed: glLighting on/off left the composed projection stale; a
texture-matrix change cleared a pending modelview/projection update;
glMaterial(GL_FRONT_AND_BACK) rewrote the op inside a display list so
replays only set the front; the local-viewer specular vector used X for
all three components.

Rasterisation rules fixed at integration (2026-09-25; found by
gl/tests/glx_prims.c against Mesa, 34% -> 0.013% tolerant-bad; details in
artifacts/gl/phase1/INTEGRATION.md):
- matrix.c glopOrtho: upstream filled the row-major M4 column-major, so
  every asymmetric glOrtho (glOrtho(0,w,h,0) of every 2D app) was
  transposed, translation in the w row. Symmetric ortho hid it.
- matrix.c glopRotate (found 2026-09-26 by gl/tests/glx_pixels.c page 4):
  the same transposition for any axis other than x, y or z, so such a
  rotation turned by -angle (glRotatef(35, 1, 1, 0)). Axis rotations -
  gears, the bench demos - were right and are unchanged.
- GL_FLAT provoking vertex (GL 1.5 table 2.12): the flat fillers read p2
  AFTER their y sort, and the quad/quad-strip/strip decompositions did not
  keep the provoking vertex in p2. vertex.c records it (gl_set_provoking);
  clip.c applies it to the triangle's three vertices and to flat lines.
- clip.c: with lighting off gl_transform_to_viewport takes the CURRENT
  colour, so clipped vertices got the last glColor; they now take their
  own (gl_zp_color). Clipped lines in select mode are selected, not drawn.
- zline.h: smooth lines started at p2's colour and stepped from p1.
- zfeatures.h: only the 16-bit output format is compiled (the others were
  dead code, and 8-bit dithering could exit(1)).
- (superseded by plan F4: GL_MODULATE and the other environments are drawn)
(Superseded 2026-09-26 by ztri.h: tier 1 no longer snaps vertices or
uses the (size - 0.5) / 2 scale for triangles, so exact-integer edges land
where GL's do and a units-only glPolygonOffset works on slanted planes.
A pixel centre exactly on a diagonal edge can still go to the other
triangle than Mesa's: the y flip of the window transform is float, so the
tie is not exact - but both paths decide it the same way.)

(Superseded 2026-09-26 by phase 3a G01, below: the per-frame and
per-vertex soft-double sites are gone.)
Not changed yet (plan stage 3): the soft-double sites TinyGL has always had
(gl_clipcode's CLIP_EPSILON, sqrt/pow in lighting, sin/cos in glRotate,
the specular table's pow; 1.0/W per vertex in gl_transform_to_viewport and
1.0/fz per triangle in ztriangle.h were float in the object code already -
GCC narrows a double division of floats - and are written 1.0f now). After --gc-sections the RV32 library
has 20 __extendsfdf2, 18 __truncdfsf2, 8 __muldf3, 3 __divdf3, 1
__floatsidf, 1 __gedf2 call sites plus pow x4, sincos x3, cos x2, sqrt x2
(objdump of gl/out-rv32/libGL.so.1.unstripped, 2026-09-25).

Phase 3a, geometry levers (2026-09-26; measurements and decisions in
artifacts/gl/phase3a/LEVERS.md):
- G01, no soft double left on a per-frame or per-vertex path. glRotate,
  GL_SPOT_CUTOFF, the spot exponent, the specular table and the fog
  factors use s31_fmath.c: sin/cos of DEGREES reduced exactly by multiples
  of 90 (<= 0.92 ulp, exact 0 and +-1 at multiples of 90), a float pow
  (<= 8.4e-6 relative) and exp (<= 1.08 ulp), measured by
  gl/tests/fmath_test.c. gl_V3_Norm and glRotate's axis use sqrtf. The
  glGet*dv widenings are bit-exact integer code (s31_float.h s31_f2d /
  s31_i2d, gl/tests/f2d_test.c: all 2^32 floats). What is left in the
  objects: the s31_d2f/f2d special-value fallbacks, gl_print_* (debug)
  and fmodf for |angle| >= 2^23 degrees.
- G02: the specular term is skipped when the material's or the light's
  specular colour is zero (bit-exact); the material caches its specular
  table; the normal matrix is the 3x3 cofactor inverse of an affine
  modelview, recomputed only when the modelview's bits change; emission +
  scene ambient and each light's ambient product are computed per state
  change; colour clamps are fmin/fmax; glColor under GL_COLOR_MATERIAL
  writes the material directly.
- G14: immediate-mode glVertex/glNormal/glColor/glTexCoord/glBegin/glEnd
  run their op directly while not compiling; list replay calls the vertex
  op directly; the strips and the fan stop copying 148-byte vertices; the
  projection's glFrustum/glOrtho zeros and an affine modelview's w row are
  skipped per vertex; glDrawElements has a 64-entry post-transform vertex
  cache; GLContext is laid out so every hot field is within the 2 kB an
  RV32 load reaches (cold arrays and the lights at the end).
- Correctness fixes found on the way:
  - glVertex4 with w != 1 (and size-4 vertex arrays): both vertex paths
    assumed w = 1 and drew the vertex at (x, y, z) instead of (x/w, ...);
    now the full product (gl/tests/glx_geo.c rows 0-1).
  - GL_LIGHT1..7 defaulted to LIGHT0's white diffuse and specular; GL
    1.3 table 6.9 says (0,0,0,1). morph3d's frames are now 0.000% from
    Mesa (were 0.016-0.034%).
  - glopDisableClientState cleared the wrong bits (unreachable: the entry
    point sets the state directly).
- Known and unchanged: the specular table quantises the highlight (a few
  pixels per lit sphere, glx_geo row 3). (Gouraud colour under differing w:
  phase 4, below.)


Phase 3a, pixel side (2026-09-26; measured on the host only, see
artifacts/gl/phase3a/LEVERS.md part B):
- Clears (zbuffer.c ZB_fill16): every 16-bit fill is aligned 32-bit stores,
  sixteen a loop turn (RV32 without D has no wider scalar store); 1.13
  instructions a store, against 1.5 for TinyGL's memset_16.
- Depth epochs (G03, s31_zepoch.c): a full glClear of depth to 1.0 usually
  writes nothing - the next frame stores every depth as TinyGL's own value
  plus a base above everything already in the buffer, so what was left
  behind compares as the clear value. Exact, not the classic ping-pong
  (which lets a pixel drawn two frames ago occlude): depth tests, stored
  values and depth read back are bit for bit the plain 16-bit ones, and no
  depth bit is given up; the rare cases where a stale pixel would not act
  as 1.0 (a GL_LESS/GEQUAL/EQUAL/NOTEQUAL fragment at the far plane) and a
  scene that no longer fits above the base are handled by rewriting the
  buffer first (materialise / demote). The state lives after the depth
  values (S31GL_DEPTH_TAIL bytes, s31gl.h), so contexts sharing a
  drawable's depth agree. S31GL_ZTRICK=0 turns it off.
- Dirty rows: with a retained colour buffer (s31gl_set_retained; the GLX
  layer sets it) a full clear writes only the rows drawn into since that
  buffer's last full clear to the same value - per colour buffer, so GLX's
  two ping-pong SHM segments each keep their own record - and a real depth
  clear only the rows drawn since the last one. Triangles record their
  rows in the fillers (ztri.h ztri_rows); lines and points their box with
  the width; pixel rectangles the whole buffer. A frame whose rows covered
  90% or more stops recording for 16 frames. S31GL_DIRTYBOX=0 turns it off.
- Fillers: the flat and Gouraud span loops do two pixels a turn with the
  odd one first and an end pointer (no count, no remainder loop to set up:
  spans are short - gears 4.8 pixels); the rows end at a depth-row pointer;
  ztri_setup sorts scalars instead of indexing stack arrays. Every output
  pixel is the same.
- Measured and not kept: 32-bit paired colour/depth stores in the flat
  filler (+6.8% instructions on gears, -33% of its stores); the x extent in
  the dirty box (+0.2-0.6% instructions for a further -20% of glxgears'
  clear stores: a board A/B decides it); the textured filler's remainder
  as an end-pointer loop (+0.1-0.4%); depth epochs by fixed halves or by
  shrinking precision (one or two apps' error against Mesa grew: geartrain
  0.030 -> 0.047%).


Phase 4 (2026-09-26; measurements in artifacts/gl/phase4/REPORT.md)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Every choice below is made once per triangle (or batch), never per pixel;
a frame that uses none of it runs the phase 3a code (gl/bench: every
frame hash the same, gears/glxgears/texobj/teapot at most +0.37%).
- F-LIN, texture filters (s31_tfilter.c; the kinds and the level chain in
  raster_sel.c zpx_prepare; the per-triangle choice zpx_tri, called by the
  general filler when ZPipe.xact says a batch has one):
  - levels > 0 are stored as uploaded (texture.c tex_level_store: each its
    own RGB565 + A8 block in GLTexture.mip, allocated at the first level
    > 0; a full chain is +33%, a texture without one pays 4 bytes;
    S31GL_MIPMAPS=0 stores none). glTexSubImage2D, glCopyTex* and
    glGetTexImage reach them.
  - GL_LINEAR: bilinear on RGB565 spread into one word (5 spare bits a
    field), 5-bit rounded weights, the A8 plane lerped alongside; the
    filtered texel feeds the unchanged texenv stages (ZPipeX.ftex, idx =
    i). REPEAT-only and general-wrap variants, with and without alpha.
  - mipmaps: rho = max(|d(u,v)/dx|, |d(u,v)/dy|) from the s/w, t/w, 1/w
    planes (perspective-correct). Review 4 R1: a triangle whose 1/w differ
    by more than ~3% takes lambda per 8-pixel block (s31_tfilter.c
    zp_run_lod: one divide a block, runs of blocks with the same levels
    form a chunk, the trilinear weight is per block); any other triangle
    once at its centroid (lambda varies < 0.09 across it). One lambda per
    triangle had a receding one-quad floor 13-16% off Mesa; per block it is
    0.01-0.34% (gl/tests/glx_floor.c in run-p4apps.sh, filt_test's
    per-pixel model). The NEAREST levels are exact from the float bits,
    the LINEAR blends use a quadratic log2. LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR trilinear
    (S31GL_TRILINEAR=0: as LINEAR_MIPMAP_NEAREST); NEAREST_MIPMAP_LINEAR
    two nearest samples blended (review 4 R2).
  - the switch to minification is Mesa's lambda > 0, not GL 1.3's c = 0.5
    for LINEAR magnification with NEAREST_MIPMAP_* (review 4 R3: the suite
    is scored against Mesa; with c = 0.5 a glx_rev cell was 99.2% off).
  - GL 1.2 texture LOD state (review 4 R4): GL_TEXTURE_MAX_LEVEL ends the
    chain (completeness and sampling), MIN_LOD / MAX_LOD clamp lambda,
    BASE_LEVEL is recorded (a value above 0 is noted once: level 0 stays
    the base); all four are queried and pushed. A level whose internal
    format differs from level 0's makes the texture incomplete (GL 1.3
    3.8.10; formats 1-4 count as their base formats).
  - a filtered texture takes the general path (tier 1 is nearest level 0);
    lines and points use the magnification filter at level 0; the pixel
    paths stay nearest. S31GL_TEXFILTER=0 draws every filter as nearest in
    level 0 on tier 1 and stores no level > 0 - exactly the pre-phase-4
    library (gl/bench filt1-4 0.638 M a frame, the NEAREST control's hash),
    the arm for a board A/B of filtered apps: gl/bench filt11 (QuakeSpasm's
    default trilinear world plus a lightmap pass) is 14.7 M a frame
    filtered, 7.6 M with it off.
  - known differences from Mesa, measured (artifacts/gl/phase4/REPORT.md):
    GL_CLAMP under a linear filter is drawn as CLAMP_TO_EDGE (the border
    colour is not blended: 68% of a glx_rev cell whose coordinates run to
    -0.25..1.25, 58% with a border texture; neither QuakeSpasm 0.96.3 nor
    TyrQuake 0.71 uses GL_CLAMP); a smooth point's coverage footprint is
    GL's clamp(size/2 + 1/2 - r), ~50% larger than llvmpipe's hard disc,
    and every covered fragment runs the stencil and depth ops (size 4:
    4,546 stencil writes against Mesa's 2,973; smooth lines match Mesa's
    footprint exactly); the long-span re-anchoring starts at 64 pixels
    (below, 40x40 quads with a 4-corner gradient are 2.4-2.9% off Mesa;
    16 or 32 would fix them and change the gears / glxgears / teapot
    frame hashes the bench pins); Mesa's 1D LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR blend
    weight differs (a glx_rev2 cell: 0.35 against GL's 0.40).
  - a colour stage nothing reads is not placed (RGB REPLACE/DECAL with no
    alpha test or alpha blend factor): -20% on the general path's
    REPLACE/DECAL spans (gl/bench feat1/feat2 texobj), same pixels.
- F-PERSP, Gouraud colour:
  - perspective: a smooth triangle whose w and colours differ enough for
    screen-affine colour to be off by 4 8-bit levels (one RGB565 green
    step) gets r/w, g/w, b/w over 1/w re-derived every 8 pixels, stepped
    along the chord: tier 1 ZB_fillTriangleSmoothPersp (LEQUAL, LESS), the
    general path's zc_smooth_pc for everything else.
  - long spans: TinyGL's packed colour steps with a truncated gradient
    (1/32 of a step, 1/16 for blue), so a 64-pixel span drifts by up to 4
    blue steps (SDL testgl's creases, glOrtho, w = 1): a smooth triangle 64
    or more pixels wide is re-anchored every 8 pixels from its integer
    planes (ZB_fillTriangleSmoothLong: LEQUAL, LESS, no depth test).
  - the test is one per smooth tier-1 triangle (gl_draw_triangle_fill_pq:
    the bits of the three 1/w and the snapped x width, one shift each);
    S31GL_PERSPCOLOR=0 turns both off.
- light.c: GL_SPOT_DIRECTION is transformed by the modelview's upper 3x3
  when specified (GL 1.3 2.13.1); TinyGL stored it as given, so a spot set
  after gluLookAt pointed elsewhere (mesa-demos teapot: 4-6% of every
  frame).
Tests: gl/tests/filt_test.c (bilinear against a float model, the mip
level rules, perspective colour, a 400-batch fuzz with canaries; host,
RV32 qemu-user and ASan/UBSan), gl/bench/filt.sh (the costs).

Phase 4, step 2 (2026-09-26): stencil, blend equations, smooth lines and
points. Measured in artifacts/gl/phase4/bench/p4s-*, smooth/ and s2final/.
None of it runs, or is
tested, on a primitive or pixel that does not use it: each is a stage of
the general path chosen at glBegin (raster_sel.c), and a frame without them
takes exactly the code it took before (gl/bench: <= +0.03% instructions,
same frame hashes).
- F8-STENCIL (s31_stencil.c, zpipe.c zs_*, raster_sel.c zs_build):
  - an 8-bit buffer only for a context with GL_STENCIL_BITS 8
    (s31gl_set_stencil_bits: GLX gives it to the STENCIL_SIZE 8 configs,
    listed after the stencil-0 ones, gl/glx/glx_config.c); the drawable's
    (s31gl_bind_stencil, shared like depth) or a private one made with the
    depth buffer. Without it the stencil test passes and nothing is
    modified (GL 1.3 4.1.5), exactly.
  - the test and ops are one table load per fragment: ZPipeX.stab[s] holds
    the value each outcome leaves (fail / depth fail / pass, through the
    write mask) and the test's result, built at state change (256 entries,
    cached by state). Eight stage variants: first in the list or after the
    alpha test / polygon stipple (GL's order), read-only or writing, with
    the depth write fused or not; the depth test runs inside it.
  - the stencil pointer is the depth pointer's offset (ZPipeX.st_zb/st_sb),
    so no span producer or runner carries one; lines point them at their
    gathered copies for the line.
  - clears honour scissor and GL_STENCIL_WRITEMASK; a full clear to the
    value of the last full clear writes only the byte range written since
    (ZStencilState in the buffer's tail; S31GL_STENCILRANGE=0: always all).
  - glDrawPixels / glReadPixels(GL_STENCIL_INDEX) and glCopyPixels(
    GL_STENCIL), with zoom, the index shift/offset and render scale
    (GL_MAP_STENCIL recorded, not applied; GL_BITMAP type not taken).
  - INCR_WRAP / DECR_WRAP (EXT_stencil_wrap, advertised).
  - memory (review 4): GLX callocs the drawable's stencil and says so
    (s31gl_stencil_zeroed), and a private one is calloc'd too, so full
    clears to 0 write nothing until something draws into it - QuakeSpasm
    asks for 8 bits and clears them every frame without a stencil test,
    and its 256-384 kB stay non-resident; the 1 kB stencil table is
    allocated at a context's first stencil batch, not in every context.
- BLEND-EQ (zpipe.c zp_out_fn): all five equations; SUBTRACT and
  REVERSE_SUBTRACT with ONE,ONE and SRC_ALPHA,ONE fused, MIN/MAX direct,
  the rest generic. The GL_CONSTANT_* factors (glBlendColor) and GL 1.4's
  factor rules. glBlendFuncSeparate's alpha factors and the alpha equation
  are recorded (glGet, glPushAttrib) and change no pixel - exact, as there
  is no destination alpha plane. Exported since SDL2 is built without its
  GL render driver (plan 4.2 option B; gl/api/mkstubs.py).
- SMOOTH (raster.c gl_aa_line / gl_aa_point, zpipe.c zv_cover): coverage
  at the pixel centre from the distance to the primitive - a line:
  clamp(w/2 + 1/2 - |d|, 0, 1) * clamp(len/2 + 1/2 - |l|, 0, min(1, len)),
  Mesa's model to the pixel (artifacts/gl/phase4/smooth/); a point:
  clamp(size/2 + 1/2 - r, 0, 1) (Mesa's llvmpipe draws smooth points as
  hard-edged disks; this follows GL). Alpha times coverage after fog,
  before the alpha test. Real widths from 1 up (granularity 1/8). With
  blending off the footprint is written opaque, as GL and Mesa do
  (S31GL_SMOOTH_NOBLEND=0: aliased then). Line stipple does not apply to
  smooth lines (noted once).
Tests: gl/tests/core_test.c (test_blend_eq, test_stencil, test_smooth),
gl/glx/test/glxtest.c (stencil_tests), gl/tests/glx_p4.c and
run-p4apps.sh (against Mesa, with mesa-demos dinoshade, dissolve,
tri-stencil, stencilwrap), gl/tests/run-stencil-pick.sh (SDL2, SDL 1.2,
freeglut get stencil 0 unless they ask), gl/bench/p4.sh (the costs).

Hot code in RAM (phase 4, lever L1: s31_ramtext.c, s31_ramtext.h,
gl/api/ramtext.list, ramtext.ld, ramtext.py; artifacts/gl/phase4/REPORT.md):
- The functions gl/api/ramtext.list names (the GL_LESS fillers and their
  setup, glVertex's transform/lighting/assembly, the triangle entry,
  glopCallList: ~10 kB) are linked as one range behind the GL stubs.
  S31GL_RAMTEXT=1 copies it at the first context creation into whole pages
  of libGL's .bss, retargets its references out of the range from a table
  build-lib.sh writes into the linked file (ramtext.py, from the linker's
  -q relocations; the build fails if the range cannot move), and makes the
  pages RX. The default is 0 until the board A/B says otherwise.
- Only the entry points in s31_rt reach the copy, all chosen at state
  changes: the fillers (raster_sel.c), the GL_FILL entry (raster_sel.c),
  glVertex (api.c, through GLContext.vtx_run, which also replaced the
  per-vertex flag test: -2 instructions a vertex) and glCallList (api.c,
  straight to glopCallList when executing). Everything else - the
  clipper, vertex arrays, rasterpos - keeps calling the XIP copy.
- On the S31 the order is load-bearing: all writes, then mprotect(RX),
  which is what makes the kernel write the D-cache back and invalidate the
  I-cache for the pages (flush_icache_pte -> esp32s31_cache_sync_for_exec);
  fence.i alone would not.
- Checks: gl/tests/run-ramtext.sh (qemu-user RV32, static and through
  musl's ld.so; the host rig; the glref suite with S31GL_RAMTEXT=1),
  gl/tests/ramtext_trace.py (where the hot blocks really run), run-san.sh.

Phase 5, O1 (2026-09-26): two texture units, the combiner, GL_ADD
(s31_mtex.c, zpipe_fused.c, zpipe_int.h, ztriangle_genmt.c;
artifacts/gl/phase5/REPORT.txt). Advertised when S31GL_MTEX is not 0:
GL_ARB_multitexture (GL_MAX_TEXTURE_UNITS 2), GL_ARB_texture_env_combine
and GL_EXT_texture_env_combine, GL_ARB_texture_env_add and
GL_EXT_texture_env_add. GL_VERSION stays 1.1; no VBO, no GLSL.
- State. Unit 0's state is where TinyGL kept its only unit's
  (current_texture, texenv_mode, texgen_*, matrix_stack[2],
  current_tex_coord), so every single-texture path reads the same fields
  as before. Unit 1's is GLContext.tu1 (GLTexUnit) and its texture matrix
  stack matrix_stack[3] (glMatrixMode(GL_TEXTURE) selects 2 + the active
  unit). A command on "the active unit" (glBindTexture, glTexEnv,
  glTexParameter, glTexImage*, glTexGen, glEnable of a texture target or
  texgen, glGet*, glIsEnabled, the texture pixel paths) runs its ordinary
  body between two tu_swap() calls when unit 1 is active, so one
  implementation serves both units; glBindTexture and glEnable/Disable of
  GL_TEXTURE_1D/2D on unit 1 set tu1 directly (once per surface in a
  multitexturing game). Client arrays: glClientActiveTexture and tc_swap(),
  unit 1's texcoord array is client state bit 0x40, fetched out of line
  (array_tex1). glPushAttrib(GL_TEXTURE_BIT/ENABLE_BIT/CURRENT_BIT) saves
  both units' records and the active unit (gl/api/gl_pushattrib.c);
  glPushClientAttrib both units' arrays. Display lists compile
  glActiveTexture and glMultiTexCoord; glClientActiveTexture executes.
- Nothing costs a frame that does not use unit 1: c->mtex_used is set by
  the first glActiveTexture / glClientActiveTexture of unit 1, and until
  then glBegin, the vertex path and gl_update_raster take the phase 4
  code (unit 1's vertex coordinate is GLVertex.tex_coord1, at the end of
  the struct, copied only by gl_vertex_indexed_mt; clip.c interpolates it
  only when vtx_extra bit 4 says so).
- The combiner. Every texture environment of a unit - the legacy modes
  and GL_COMBINE - becomes a ZComb program (raster_sel.c comb_prog):
  per channel class a function (REPLACE MODULATE ADD ADD_SIGNED
  INTERPOLATE SUBTRACT), three sources (TEXTURE CONSTANT PRIMARY_COLOR
  PREVIOUS) with their operands, and a scale shift (RGB_SCALE /
  ALPHA_SCALE 1 2 4 -> 0 1 2). The generic stage zc_comb evaluates it on
  a 32-pixel chunk in 8-bit integers: products MUL8 (a*(b+1)>>8, the
  texenv stages' own, zpipe_int.h), ADD_SIGNED a+b-128, INTERPOLATE
  MUL8(a,c)+MUL8(b,255-c), SUBTRACT a-b, then the shift and a clamp to
  0..255. The primary
  colour is saved (zc_saveprim) only when unit 1 reads it after unit 0
  replaced it; a class nothing reads is not computed (comb_reads). A
  legacy mode on unit 0 alone still takes the phase 4 stages. RGB
  textures read alpha 255 whatever the sampler left in the alpha array.
- Stage order with unit 1: [stencil][stipple][col][saveprim][tex0]
  [env0/comb0][tex1][comb1][spec][fog][cover][alpha][zwrite/stencil][out].
  Unit 1 has its own texel index stages (zt1_*: REPEAT/CLAMP per axis)
  and filtered samplers (s31_tfilter.c: every NEAREST/LINEAR/mipmap
  sampler exists for both units; zp_run_lod_mt keeps both units' LOD),
  its own interpolants (ZSpan sz1/tz1, ZP_N_ST1, ztriangle_genmt.c: the
  general filler compiled a second time in its own translation unit so
  the one-unit filler keeps its phase 4 code), and lines, points, smooth
  primitives, glBitmap and glDrawPixels are textured by it too (the raster
  position keeps unit 1's coordinates).
- Fused fillers (zpipe_fused.c, S31GL_FUSED=0 turns them off). When the
  stage list and the two programs are exactly QuakeSpasm's r_world.c case
  1 (lightmapped world: unit 0 REPLACE or MODULATE of an opaque texture,
  unit 1 MODULATE, or GL_COMBINE MODULATE with RGB_SCALE 2, of the
  lightmap; flat or smooth primary; any sampler) or r_alias.c case 1
  (alias models: unit 0 MODULATE of the skin by the vertex colour, unit 1
  GL_ADD of the fullbright mask, blended or not), zpf_select replaces the
  combiner and output stages by one stage that calls the same texel stages
  and then does the arithmetic of the general stages in one loop, from the
  same macros. World RGB products come from 5 KB of product tables built
  on first use (per context, freed with it). With both units NEAREST, a
  REPEAT wrap and a known depth state, the world filler also walks both
  textures and tests depth inline (zf_world_nn0/1/2). Every fused filler
  is gated bit-identical to the general stage list, colour and depth, by
  gl/tests/fused_test.c (host and RV32; the general arm is a context with
  S31GL_FUSED=0).
- Knobs: S31GL_MTEX=0 (one unit, the phase 4 extension string: QuakeSpasm
  then takes its no-multitexture passes), S31GL_FUSED=0 (general path
  only). tgl_fused_stats / s31gl_fused_stats count fused batches.
- Tests: gl/tests/glx_mtex.c pages 1-5 against Mesa (run-mtex.sh, in
  run-3a.sh), core_test test_mtex (exact 565 results, errors, lists,
  arrays, glDrawPixels, push/pop), fused_test (the gate), and the
  QuakeSpasm trace (tools/glref/gltrace/compare-qs.sh against Mesa).
- Mesa (llvmpipe) differences seen while testing, none of them in ours:
  it accepts GL_ONE as a combiner source and glActiveTexture /
  glMultiTexCoord of units past GL_MAX_TEXTURE_UNITS without an error;
  its glBitmap/glDrawPixels with unit 1 enabled needed a glFlush to show
  (glx_mtex page 5), so glDrawPixels through unit 1 is checked exactly in
  core_test instead (artifacts/gl/phase5/probe/).
- Cost: .text 170 -> 209 kB (Buildroot flags), stripped 276 -> 317 kB, of
  which the second unit's filtered samplers are 11.6 kB, the fused fillers
  6.2 kB and the two-unit general filler 3.8 kB. GLContext 5996 -> 7132
  bytes, GLVertex 148 -> 164 bytes; hot fields still end below 2 KB
  (mtex_used at 1692).

Phase 5, O2 (2026-09-26): fused fillers for every per-pixel signature
QuakeSpasm 0.96.3 still sent through the general stage list, and the
filtered path's cost (zpipe_fused.c, s31_tfilt_int.h; report
artifacts/gl/phase5/O2-REPORT.md). No extension, no GL state and no
pixel changes: every fused filler is gated bit-identical to the general
list it replaces (gl/tests/fused_test.c, 19 scenarios, host and RV32;
gl/tests/run-qsr-fused.sh, every full frame of ten QuakeSpasm traces).
- Filtered world (ZF_WORLD with GL_LINEAR lightmaps, both units REPEAT,
  depth LEQUAL + write): zf_world_x reads which texel stage the per-triangle
  / per-block level choice placed in unit 0's slot, once per chunk, and
  runs the loop made for it (nearest in level 0 or d, nearest-mipmap-
  linear, bilinear, trilinear); each loop tests depth first and samples
  only the fragments that pass (31% of QuakeSpasm's trilinear world pixels
  are hidden), with the stages' own macros (s31_tfilt_int.h, now shared)
  and walks. A bilinear sample keeps the last 2x2 square (the lightmap,
  magnified, hits 79% on the QuakeSpasm trace) and then needs one multiply per horizontal
  lerp (32 a + SRND + (b - a) w is a (32 - w) + b w + SRND mod 2^32, and
  the true value is below 2^32). Trilinear's finer level is sampled
  uncached (86% of its squares are new). Two passes for bilinear and
  trilinear (depth + lightmap, then unit 0), one for the nearest kinds:
  measured, each the fewest instructions. The runners call it directly
  (ZPipeX.run_mt / run_lod_mt: zp_run_mt_direct, zp_run_lod_mt_direct -
  no depth stage call, no list walk), as they do the nearest world
  filler.
- One-unit signatures (zf1_*, zf1_pick): the status bar and view blend
  (SRC_ALPHA / ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA of a texel or a flat colour: per-alpha
  tables of MUL8 of each field's expansion, 192 B; an opaque status bar
  stores the texel), HUD pictures and characters (alpha GREATER), fences,
  the console, water, alias models without a fullbright texture (COMBINE
  MODULATE x 2), particles, the glow pass, and for a Quake without
  multitexture the lightmap passes (DST_COLOR / SRC_COLOR, ZERO /
  SRC_COLOR) and alias passes. Each runs the batch's own colour and texel
  stages, then one loop of the texenv, alpha test, depth write and blend
  arithmetic (zpipe_int.h). A texel stage that is bilinear in level 0 with
  no per-triangle choice is replaced, for the REPLACE signatures, by
  zf_bil0_*: exact shortcuts when a weight is 0 or 32 (LERP(x, y, 0) is x,
  LERP(x, y, 32) is y) - one row's lerp, one column's, or one texel.
  QuakeSpasm's status bar is 1:1 vertically and 320 pixels from 256 texels
  across (GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE).
- The trilinear level code (zpx_code2, once per 8-pixel block) has
  zpx_code's LML / NML steps inline: GL's default MIN_LOD / MAX_LOD clamp
  is the identity for a finite lambda, the rest is the same arithmetic.
- S31GL_FUSED=0 turns all of it off (the gates' reference arm).
  s31gl_fused_stats has eight counters now (5 one-unit, 6 filtered world).
- Diagnostics: gl/bench/qscensus.sh (a -DS31GL_CENSUS bench build,
  s31_census.c: pixels per stage list), gl/bench/pcannot.py (instructions
  per address of one function). Neither is in the shipped library.
- Cost: .text 209,436 -> 223,790 B (Buildroot flags; 3 kB of it cold
  selection code), zpipe_fused.o 6.2 -> 18.2 kB. Other heap +192 B (the
  blend tables, at the first such batch). ZPipeX +24 B (off the hot 2 kB).

Phase 5, P5c (2026-09-26): precision, texel storage, fused 8-bit fillers
(s31_tex8.c, zpipe_fused8.h, s31_tfilt_int.h; report
artifacts/gl/phase5/p5c/REPORT-P5C.txt, final numbers
artifacts/gl/phase5/REPORT.txt).
- Rounding like Mesa: every float / 8-bit to 565 conversion, the clear
  colour, glColor to the fragment colour, glDrawPixels, the texenv and
  blend products (div255r MUL8 / MIX8 / MULS8, ADDS8). glx_prec 72.94 ->
  99.35% of the values exact vs Mesa (gated in run-3a at >= 99.3).
  -DS31GL_P4ARITH builds the phase-4 arithmetic (the bar-2 compat arm).
- Texel storage chosen per texture at its first level (S31GL_TEX8, default
  1): greyscale RGBA (r == g == b) as L8 with an alpha mode of none / 1-bit
  / A8; <= 256 distinct colours as P8 indices + an RGBA8 palette; opaque
  RGBA without the A8 plane; the rest RGB565 (+A8). S31GL_TEX8=0 is the
  phase-4 565 storage, =2 the unpacked 32-bit reference (TGL_ST_W32) the
  fused_test and qsr-fused gates compare the 8-bit fetch against,
  bit-identical. See the KNOWN DEVIATION note at the top of s31_tex8.c: a
  sub-image an L8 / P8 texture cannot hold converts it to 565 (review S3).
- The trilinear lerp (LERPT) adds a bias of 12/32 in G and B and 11/32 in R
  instead of rounding. That was tuned against the suite bar on three apps
  (fire, ipers, teapot; artifacts/gl/phase5/p5c/x4), and the comment in
  s31_tfilt_int.h calls it fragile. S31GL_FILT8=1 (8-bit filters on 565
  textures) is the honest-precision arm at +44% instructions; off.
- Phase 5 review O7 (LIBGL-OPPORTUNITIES.md): no per-frame or per-vertex
  path calls libc memcpy / memcmp / memset at 64 bytes or more (musl's ESP
  PIE path, which bounces off the lent CPU). zgl.h s31_wcopy / s31_wdiff
  are word loops with an opaque word (an empty asm) so GCC's loop
  distribution cannot turn them back into calls: the modelview-inverse
  cache in glBegin (64 B copy + compare), the glDrawElements vertex cache
  hit / save (the 148-B GLVertex prefix), glLoadMatrixf / glMultMatrixf
  (64 B, RV32 only: GLParam is 8 B on a 64-bit host), the S31Unpack copy
  per glTexImage / glTexSubImage (68 B), aligned client rows in t8_row;
  the L8 lightmap update no longer clears the unused 1 kB palette hash.
  gl/tests/memchk-pie.sh lists every mem* call with a constant size >= 64
  in the RV32 library; what remains is setup, glXChoose*, the pixel paths
  (glBitmap, glDrawPixels, glRasterPos) and the P8 palette scan.
  QuakeSpasm trace: -0.4% / -0.7% default, -0.8% / -1.6% TEXFILTER=0, frame
  hashes identical.
- s31_cap_index (glEnable / glDisable) has a 64-slot direct-mapped memo,
  verified against caps[] (review P5: 0.23 M instructions a QuakeSpasm
  frame in the linear search).
- Cost: .text 223,790 (O2) -> 300,130 B, stripped 333,440 -> 411,264 B
  (Buildroot flags, gl/bench/brsize.sh); 83 of the 115 fused / 8-bit
  functions do not run on the QuakeSpasm default or TEXFILTER=0 replays.
- Not done, owner decisions: GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE stays 256 (TyrQuake 0.71
  GL's 320x24 status bar draws white: it does not clamp; review S1), the
  8-bit storage and rounded blend's cost on small textures and
  glCopyTexSubImage2D (review P2, bench limits over), per-level texel kinds
  (review P4).

Phase 5, fix 2 (2026-09-26; artifacts/gl/phase5/fix2/REPORT.txt): the
feature-free bench regressions, GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE 512, .text.
- Storage (s31_tex8.c t8_kind): a colour RGB / RGBA image whose every
  colour is exact in RGB565 (UNPACK(PACK(c)) == c: 0 and 255 always) is
  stored 565, not P8 - the texels read back identically, and tier 1 and
  the phase-4 stages fetch it without the palette load (texobj +10% ->
  -0.5% vs phase 4). Grey images stay L8 (a black lightmap keeps its 8
  bits). Such a texture carries
  GLTexture.x565: filtered, it takes the 8-bit filters (raster_sel.c
  UNIT_W8, as S31GL_FILT8=1 does for every 565 texture), so its filtered
  pixels are the P8 storage's exactly - the first cut without the flag
  sent it through phase 4's 565 filter and glx_mtex page 3 went from
  2.58% / 0.03% (strict / tolerant) to 3.99% / 1.44%, a FAIL.
- glCopyTexSubImage2D / glCopyTexImage2D into a 565 level (st565_rows):
  the colour buffer's 565 values are stored as they are (no pixel
  transfer; the 8-bit expansion and T565 are inverse in both arithmetics).
  A copy over the whole of an RGB / RGBA texture's only level converts an
  L8 / P8 texture to 565 first (gl_tex8_sub): no texel is left to
  requantise, and every later copy is the direct store instead of the
  statistics pass - pix6 0.918 -> 0.087 M (phase 4 0.666). Measured cost:
  such a texture, filtered, now takes phase 4's 565 filter on the
  replicated expansion instead of the 8-bit filter on s31_c5to8's rounded
  one - glx_mtex page 4 1.421% -> 1.426% strict, 220 -> 221 px tolerant
  (still PASS). A partial copy or a mipmapped texture keeps the rules.
- SRC_ALPHA / ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA (zpipe.c zo_sa_omsa): a chunk of one
  alpha (tested a word at a time) takes the destination terms from
  zf_btab's tables and the source terms from a 256-entry MUL8 table for
  that alpha (ZPipeX.satab, 256 B at the first such chunk); alpha 255 is
  the store. Other chunks prepare each pixel's two factors once
  (MUL8K_PREP / MUL8K: round(n / 255) = (257 n + 32896) >> 16, checked
  for every n <= 70000). zo_sa_one and the (reverse) subtract pairs
  prepare the factor once per pixel. pix2 6.14 -> 5.38 M (phase 4 5.43).
- div255r is (n + 128) * 257 >> 16 with 257 in an opaque register
  (zp_k257): one multiply instead of a shift and an add; the same value
  for every n <= 70000.
- GL_MAX_TEXTURE_SIZE 512 (zgl.h TGL_TEX_MAX; owner decision): TyrQuake
  0.71 GL does not clamp its uploads, and its 320x24 status bar is a
  512x32 image. Proxies and GL_INVALID_VALUE follow it (1024 is refused,
  level 10 is invalid). The s/t fixed point keeps F + ws + hs <= 22, so a
  512 x 512 texture has 4 fraction bits (bilinear weights in 16 steps,
  not 32); nothing else in the fillers depended on 256. The s31_tex8.c
  row buffers are 512 wide (2 kB on the stack each).
- Removed: the RGB565-on-8-bit-filter world loops (zf8_wx_*_c565,
  S31GL_FILT8=1 only, 5.9 kB) and the any-kind bilinear picture shortcut
  (zf8_bil0_gen, 3.5 kB; no QuakeSpasm replay ran it): those batches
  take zf8_world_11 / the texel stage, the same pixels.
